	Well, let me put it this way... if Juiblex engulfs you, there's
a trick with a normally non-combat item that will both free you and
instantly reduce him to 1 HP. I usually don't bother, because when I
meet him in Gehennom, with endgame weapons, it's generally more
efficient to just beat him to death than to take the four turns
necessary to get said item out of my bag, use it on him, hit him for the
last HP, and return the item to my bag.

	And that's assuming that he even engulfs me. He's slow; I'm
normally very fast by that point. He frequently doesn't even get a
chance to *do* anything. He 'ports in next to me, and I dice him before
he gets another action.

	If you don't have means of curing sickness (and if you meet him
in his home swamp, #praying is not an option), he can be a serious
threat, but otherwise he's pretty much a joke, even for an
early-to-midgame character.

